    "question": "What exact visual values must all screens and components reuse?",
    "status": "DRAFT, proposed by UX (UX-005-01) at Stage 5 for the owner's selection; not selected. Values follow the main recommendation of analysis/prototyping/ui-ux-decision.md (responsive web, utilitarian style) and its first candidate palette P1 Slate Blue. Nothing here is approved until the owner records an explicit Stage 5 decision.",
    "ownership": "Stage 5 UX author drafts the foundation; Stage 6 maintains extensions. The owner decides at Stages 5 and 8.",
    "modes": "Light and dark themes are separate named tokens: color.light.* and color.dark.* with identical suffixes. ui-design-system.md binds the light names; the dark theme substitutes the color.dark token with the same suffix.",
    "units": "motion.*-ms values are milliseconds (number type). Dimensions use rem so that user text-size settings scale the interface.",
    "consumption": "The catalogue uses property=token.name bindings. audit:prototype checks types, aliases, pins and references once a manifest exists; rendered tests check visual correctness.",
    "foundation": "The canonical foundation digest is printed by node analysis/tools/ui-design-system.js; it is recorded as proposed, not as the owner pin, until the owner selects.",
    "extensions": "Empty at Stage 5. Stage 6 adds only scope-needed tokens within an approved foundation."
  },
